1 Introduction
**************

Autoslip Roam is an Emacs package that brings Niklas Luhmann's
folgezettel (follow-up slip) system to org-roam.  The package
automatically manages bidirectional links between parent and child notes
based on their folgezettel addresses.

1.1 What is a Folgezettel?
==========================

A folgezettel is a sequential numbering system used in the Zettelkasten
(slip-box) method.  Each note has an address that encodes its position
in a hierarchy of ideas.  For example:

   • ‘1.’ - A root note (first topic); the trailing period is the
     canonical marker for a root
   • ‘1.2’ - Second subtopic of note 1
   • ‘1.2a’ - First branch from 1.2
   • ‘1.2a3’ - Third continuation of 1.2a

   Legacy titles without the trailing period on the root (e.g., ‘1
Crystallography’) are still recognized and treated as equivalent to the
canonical ‘1.’ form.

1.2 Features
============

   • Automatic parent backlink generation when creating child notes
   • Automatic forward link insertion in parent notes
   • Bidirectional cross-linking when manually inserting links
   • Validation to prevent invalid addresses
   • Duplicate index detection
   • Suggestions for next child address
   • Database synchronization for immediate link visibility
   • Navigation commands to jump to the parent, list direct children, or
     show the whole vault as a folgezettel-ordered tree
   • Reparent commands that move a note (or an entire subtree) to a new
     folgezettel address and keep titles, links, and filenames in sync
   • Chain-of-thought commands that render the path from a note to its
     root in a dedicated buffer and can insert that path into the
     current note
   • Cross-linked chain-of-thought command that shows the folgezettel
     context of every note linked under Cross References
   • Optional property-drawer link-storage mode for a quieter note body
   • Transient menu that shows the chain of thought, the neighboring
     notes, and the children of the current note at once
   • Browser dashboard that writes the whole hierarchy to one HTML page
   • Repair command that adds every missing parent or child link in the
     vault
   • Command that links a root note back to the index of indices
   • Subtree note generator that turns an outline of addressed headlines
     into linked notes in one step
   • Lisp entry point for creating a child note from other packages


