11 Repairing Links
******************

A vault that was built before automatic linking, or edited by hand, can
have notes without their parent or child links.

     C-u M-x autoslip-roam-repair-links    report only
     M-x autoslip-roam-repair-links        report, ask once, then repair

   The command compares every note that has an address with its parent
note and lists what is missing in the ‘*Autoslip Repair*’ buffer.  A
line that starts with ‘B’ is a note without its link to the parent.  A
line that starts with ‘F’ is a parent without its link to the note.
Nothing is changed until you answer the one question.  Links that are
already there are left alone, so the command is safe to run more than
once.  Notes whose parent does not exist are skipped, because there is
nothing to link them to.  Back up or commit your vault before the first
repair.

11.1 Linking Root Notes to the Index
====================================

A root note has no parent, so it has no parent link.  To link a root
note back to the index of indices instead, use:

     M-x autoslip-roam-add-backlink-from-root-to-00-index
     C-u M-x autoslip-roam-add-backlink-from-root-to-00-index

   The first form links the current root note.  The second form links
every root note.  The index of indices is the note whose title carries
the address in ‘autoslip-roam-index-address’, ‘"00.0"’ by default.  The
link is placed where a parent link goes and shows the title of the index
note.  Only the root note is changed.


